      "llm_score": 3,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "Two assessments claim more than the project supports.\n▎ (1) original_substitution says \"original record images/captures used throughout … no index-only derivatives relied upon\". Every log entry (log_001–log_007) is a record_search index hit, and nothing the agent read shows an image was viewed. This is a claim of work that didn't happen.\n▎ (2) goal_alignment says the marriage record \"consistently name[s] … Alan's parents\". A 1926 marriage cannot name a child born in 1936. It shows the couple married before his birth, which is indirect evidence. The direct evidence of parentage is the census \"son\" entries and the obituary.\n▎ The other five criteria are grounded in the project."
    },
    {
